flowchart TB
    accTitle: YourSafe components and local data paths
    accDescr: The desktop runs WinUI views and Windows adapters over platform-neutral Presentation orchestration and the Core vault. The optional TypeScript extension reaches the running desktop via Native Messaging and a standalone NativeHost pipe relay. The separate development HTTP API shares hashing implementations only. Vault files and backups are local; transport arrows indicate runtime calls rather than project references.
    subgraph desktop["YourSafe.exe - desktop process"]
        ui["WinUI 3\nViews, dialogs and Windows lifecycle"] --> flow["Presentation\nViewModels + AppFlowCoordinator"]
        flow --> runner["VaultOperationRunner\nSerialize Core calls off the UI thread"]
        runner --> core["Core VaultService\nValidation, session, crypto and imports"]
        ui --> platform["Windows adapters\nClipboard, pickers and approval dialog"]
        pipe["AutofillPipeServer\nValidate peer and protocol"] --> flow
    end
    core --> files[("Local vault directory\n.config + encrypted .storage\nPaired snapshots and journal")]:::encrypted
    core --> backup[("Encrypted external backup\nUser-selected file + separate passphrase")]:::encrypted
    subgraph browser["Optional browser integration"]
        popup["Popup + worker\nAccount selection and target checks"] --> content["Content script\nExplicit fill in top-level page"]
        popup -->|Native Messaging stdin/stdout| host["YourSafe.NativeHost.exe\nStandalone framing and pipe relay"]
    end
    host -->|Current-user named pipe| pipe
    api["PasswordTool.Api\nSeparate local-development HTTP process"] --> hashing["Core hashing registry + inspector\nShared with desktop Hash Tool"]
    flow --> hashing
    classDef encrypted fill:#eff6ff,stroke:#2563eb,color:#0f172a
